# **Overview on Locators with Examples – Part 1 | Playwright Telugu**

## What are Locators in Playwright?\*\*

"Locators are used to identify web elements and perform actions on them. Playwright provides different locator methods like `getByRole()`, `getByText()`, `getByLabel()`, `getByPlaceholder()`, and `getByTestId()`. We use them to interact with elements and perform validations."

Playwright lo user-facing locators like `getByRole()` and `getByLabel()` prefer chestham because they are generally more reliable and readable.
According to the Playwright documentation you shared, there are **7 main built-in recommended locator methods**.

## **7 Playwright Locator Methods**

| No. | Locator              | Purpose                                 |
| --- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| 1   | `getByRole()`        | Locate by accessibility role and name   |
| 2   | `getByText()`        | Locate by text content                  |
| 3   | `getByLabel()`       | Locate form control by associated label |
| 4   | `getByPlaceholder()` | Locate input by placeholder             |
| 5   | `getByAltText()`     | Locate element by alternative text      |
| 6   | `getByTitle()`       | Locate element by title attribute       |
| 7   | `getByTestId()`      | Locate element by `data-testid`         |

## **Simple examples**

```
// 1. Role
page.getByRole("button", { name: "Login" });

// 2. Text
page.getByText("Welcome");

// 3. Label
page.getByLabel("Username");

// 4. Placeholder
page.getByPlaceholder("Enter email");

// 5. Alt text
page.getByAltText("Company Logo");

// 6. Title
page.getByTitle("Close");

// 7. Test ID
page.getByTestId("login-button");
```

