```

Telugu: `data-testid` attribute use chesi element ni identify chestham.

## **8.&#x20;**`locator()`**&#x20;– CSS Selector**

CSS selector use chesi elements ni identify cheyyachu.

HTML:

```
<input id="username" />
```

Playwright:

```
await page.locator("#username").fill("Satya");
```

Some common CSS selectors:

| Selector              | Meaning                |
| --------------------- | ---------------------- |
| `#username`           | ID                     |
| `.login-btn`          | Class                  |
| `input`               | Tag name               |
| `input[name="email"]` | Attribute              |
| `div button`          | Div lopala unna button |

## **9. Complete real-time example**

```
import { test, expect } from "@playwright/test";

test("Login functionality", async ({ page }) => {

  await page.goto("https://your-app-url.com");

  // Enter username
  await page.getByLabel("Username").fill("Satya");

  // Enter password
  await page.getByPlaceholder("Enter password").fill("Test123");

  // Click login button
  await page.getByRole("button", { name: "Login" }).click();

  // Verify dashboard
  await expect(
    page.getByText("Dashboard")
  ).toBeVisible();

});
```

Note: Ivi example locators. Mee application HTML and actual labels batti locators change avuthayi.

